    "figure": "figure5_independent_validation",
    "title": "Donor-separated extension",
    "caption": "A, The separate GSE194122 extension selects its panel on three discovery donors, estimates degree controls on two different reference donors and evaluates five held-out donors. Its panel has 1,200 genes and 350 TFs; each donor contributes 332 cells with identical metadata-only type quotas. This split is separate from the corrective brain analysis. B, Actual saved finite-pair coverage is shown for every evaluation donor and each of six readouts. C, Independent verification certifies all 30 inference tasks, but only five tasks from donor 16710 satisfy 100% finite frozen-pair coverage. The other 25 tasks are ineligible, not negative effect findings; every task passed the 90% minimum gene-coverage gate. D, Actual observed partial Spearman alignment for the five admitted readouts from donor 16710 under separate reference-degree, own-degree and no-degree controls. Each point uses the saved restricted row. The observed graph is shared across restricted and unrestricted null modes; their stored observed effects agree within 1e-12. The complete independently verified BMMC analysis measures 30 registered slots and retains 150 untestable slots administratively at correction input p=1 in the full 180-slot family. Untestable slots are not measured p=1 or zero effects. Pooled IUT-BY across all measured reference/own/none degree specifications and restricted/unrestricted nulls has 0 measured rows with q<0.05. The smallest measured pooled IUT-BY q is 0.103913059; 1 measured rows have pooled Holm p<0.05. The Holm row for scGPT, donor 16710, none degree mode and unrestricted null has observed partial rho -0.02381883092, raw pIUT 0.0001 and pooled Holm p 0.018. A negative observed alignment is not positive biological support. Pooled IUT-BY and Holm probabilities are reported in this caption and the full archive; panel D displays observed effects without confidence intervals or significance markers. Eligibility does not establish replication success. No donor confidence intervals, donor-population superiority or never-pretrained status are asserted.",
